# <type>(<scope>): <subject> (max 50 chars)
# |<----  Using a Maximum Of 50 Characters  ---->|


# Explain why this change is being made (max 72 chars per line)
# |<----   Try To Limit Each Line to a Maximum Of 72 Characters   ---->|

# Provide links or keys to any relevant tickets, articles or other resources
# Example: Github issue #23

# --- COMMIT END ---
# Type can be:
#   feat     (new feature)
#   fix      (bug fix)
#   refactor (refactoring code)
#   style    (formatting, missing semicolons, etc; no code change)
#   docs     (changes to documentation)
#   test     (adding or refactoring tests; no production code change)
#   chore    (updating grunt tasks etc; no production code change)
#   perf     (performance improvement)
#
# Scope is optional and can be anything specifying the place of the commit change.
# Examples: css, js, api, database, etc.
#
# Subject should use imperative tone and should not end with a period.
# Examples: "add feature" not "adds feature" or "added feature"
#
# Remember:
# - Separate subject from body with a blank line
# - Subject line: max 50 characters
# - Body: wrap at 72 characters
# - Use the body to explain what and why vs. how
# - Use the imperative mood in the subject line

